1
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:03,710
Previously on Friends:

2
00:00:03,870 --> 00:00:05,440
Erica, are you okay?

3
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,640
Yeah, you know, maybe I ate too much.

4
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:11,420
I keep getting these stomachaches. They come and go, like, every few minutes.

5
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:17,470
-Oh, my God. -Relax, we'll just get her some antacids.

6
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:20,600
She doesn't have a stomachache! She's in labor!

7
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:21,810
Oh, my God!

8
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:23,930
If you think that I didn't say goodbye...

9
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:27,520
...because you don't mean as much to me as everybody else, you're wrong.

10
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:29,480
It's because you mean more to me.

11
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:31,570
-Rach! -What?

12
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:56,360
Hey.

13
00:00:58,290 --> 00:01:01,260
Go back to sleep. I have to go home.

14
00:01:01,310 --> 00:01:04,890
Oh, God. This was amazing.

15
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:07,450
It really was.

16
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:10,430
You've learned some new moves.

17
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:15,280
Yeah, well, this guy at work gave me "Sex for Dummies"

18
00:01:15,330 --> 00:01:16,520
as a joke.

19
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:18,820
- Who's laughing now? - I am.

20
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,650
Friends S10E17E18 The Last One

21
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:13,520
Breathe...

22
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:16,590
Okay. Good.

23
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:18,660
Next time, can I say "breathe"?

24
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,700
No. Last time, you said it like Dracula,

25
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:22,470
and it scared her.

26
00:02:23,510 --> 00:02:25,450
Can I get you anything? You want some more ice chips?

27
00:02:25,450 --> 00:02:26,570
No, I'm okay.

28
00:02:26,570 --> 00:02:28,320
All right. I'll be right back.

29
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:33,350
- Where you going? - To use the bathroom.

30
00:02:33,350 --> 00:02:36,740
- You can't leave me alone with her. - What?

31
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:40,100
This is exactly the kind of social situation...

32
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:42,660
...that I am not comfortable with.

33
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:46,710
What kind of social situation are you comfortable with?

34
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:50,840
It's just that we've never spent any time, you know, alone together.

35
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,480
You'll be fine.

36
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:54,730
You won't, but I'll be back in two minutes.

37
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:56,130
Okay.

38
00:03:03,070 --> 00:03:07,500
So any plans for the summer?

39
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:12,490
I don't know. Maybe church camp.

40
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,040
May not want to mention this.

41
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:24,600
So you ever wonder which is worse?

42
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:28,170
You know, going through labor or getting kicked in the nuts?

43
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:32,910
- What? - Oh, it's just interesting.

44
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:35,060
Because no one will ever know

45
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:37,950
because no one can experience both.

46
00:03:41,650 --> 00:03:45,190
One of life's great unanswerable questions.

47
00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:48,510
Who knows? Maybe there's something

48
00:03:48,510 --> 00:03:51,350
even more painful than those things.

49
00:03:54,310 --> 00:03:56,010
Like this.

50
00:04:02,710 --> 00:04:03,890
- Come in. - Morning.

51
00:04:03,890 --> 00:04:06,000
- Hey. - What's that?

52
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,290
Oh, it's my housewarming present for Monica and Chandler.

53
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:12,970
That's a baby chick and duck.

54
00:04:12,970 --> 00:04:16,070
And I named them Chick Jr. And Duck Jr.

55
00:04:16,570 --> 00:04:18,590
I did not see that coming.

56
00:04:19,430 --> 00:04:20,840
They'll love it at that new house.

57
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:22,440
It has that big backyard.

58
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:23,440
When they're old,

59
00:04:23,450 --> 00:04:24,750
they'll go to that farm...

60
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:27,520
...that Chandler took the other chick and duck to.

61
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:30,730
- Yes. - Yeah.

62
00:04:30,730 --> 00:04:32,560
It's a shame people can't visit there.

63
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,700
That is the rule though.

64
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:40,950
Guess what. You're almost an uncle.

65
00:04:40,950 --> 00:04:41,570
What?

66
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:43,170
Erica went into labor last night.

67
00:04:43,170 --> 00:04:44,900
Monica and Chandler are at the hospital right now.

68
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:48,240
- Oh, my God! - I have a feeling it's gonna be a girl.

69
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:50,850
Phoebe, you were sure Ben was gonna be a girl.

70
00:04:50,850 --> 00:04:52,900
Have you seen him throw a ball?

71
00:04:55,910 --> 00:04:59,640
- Is Rachel here? - I think she's still asleep.

72
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:01,060
How did it go with you guys last night?

73
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:03,190
She seemed pretty pissed at you.

74
00:05:03,270 --> 00:05:06,560
We worked things out.

75
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,080
What's that smile?

76
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,740
Did something happen with you two?

77
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:13,300
Hey, I'm not one to kiss and tell.

78
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:15,880
But I'm also not one to have sex and shut up.

79
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:17,720
We totally did it.

80
00:05:18,940 --> 00:05:20,480
Oh, my God. You and Rachel?

81
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:22,320
I know, it's pretty great.

82
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:23,460
So, what does that mean?

83
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:24,950
Are you guys getting back together?

84
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:26,620
Oh, I don't know.

85
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:28,290
We didn't really get to talk.

86
00:05:28,290 --> 00:05:30,090
But do you want to get back together?

87
00:05:30,090 --> 00:05:31,570
I don't know.

88
00:05:32,350 --> 00:05:33,580
It was incredible.

89
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:36,160
I mean, it just felt so right.

90
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:37,950
When I was holding her,

91
00:05:37,950 --> 00:05:40,760
I mean, I never wanted to let her go.

92
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:45,070
Know what? Yeah, I do. I want to be together.

93
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:50,860
So is she still going to Paris?

94
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,790
Wow, I hadn't thought of that. I hope not.

95
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:56,550
This is, like, the best day ever. Ever.

96
00:05:56,550 --> 00:05:58,050
You guys might get back together.

97
00:05:58,050 --> 00:05:59,820
Monica and Chandler get their baby.

98
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:01,060
There are chicks and ducks...

99
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:03,000
...in the world again.

100
00:06:03,850 --> 00:06:06,320
I feel like I'm in a musical.

101
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:13,990
Morning.

102
00:06:13,990 --> 00:06:16,000
Guess you'll never know how it ends.

103
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,140
- Hey. - Hi.

104
00:06:19,150 --> 00:06:22,240
- Hi. How'd you sleep? - Good. You?

105
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:24,830
- Good. - I'll bet you did.

106
00:06:27,790 --> 00:06:29,510
Would you guys mind giving us a minute?

107
00:06:29,510 --> 00:06:32,090
Sure. Just keep an eye on the chick and duck.

108
00:06:32,090 --> 00:06:34,200
Chick and the duck? Didn't they die--?

109
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:40,220
Dive. Yeah, they dove. Headfirst into fun on the farm.

110
00:06:47,550 --> 00:06:48,980
So....

111
00:06:51,330 --> 00:06:54,660
- Morning. - You too.

112
00:06:55,370 --> 00:06:56,620
Last night was just wonderful.

113
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:58,700
Oh, it really was.

114
00:06:59,330 --> 00:07:01,490
I woke up today with a big smile in my face.

115
00:07:01,490 --> 00:07:03,800
I know, me too. It was....

116
00:07:03,890 --> 00:07:06,240
You know, it was one of those things

117
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,770
you think is never going to happen.

118
00:07:07,770 --> 00:07:09,260
And then it does,

119
00:07:09,270 --> 00:07:11,890
and it's everything you want it to be.

120
00:07:11,970 --> 00:07:14,740
I know. It was just....

121
00:07:16,430 --> 00:07:18,980
It's just the perfect way to say goodbye.

122
00:07:27,510 --> 00:07:28,990
Just a little bit more, honey.

123
00:07:28,990 --> 00:07:30,620
Oh, man, this hurts!

124
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:32,350
Is it really that bad?

125
00:07:32,350 --> 00:07:33,790
I think it's time to kick you in the nuts

126
00:07:33,790 --> 00:07:35,930
and see which is worse.

127
00:07:38,410 --> 00:07:40,420
The baby's head is crowning.

128
00:07:41,110 --> 00:07:42,600
Oh, my God!

129
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:45,830
That is the most beautiful top of a head I have ever seen.

130
00:07:45,830 --> 00:07:49,500
- Chandler, you have to see this. - I'm okay.

131
00:07:50,270 --> 00:07:52,050
Chandler. You don't want to miss this.

132
00:07:52,050 --> 00:07:53,610
This is the birth of your child.

133
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:56,570
- It's the miracle of life. - All right.

134
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:02,030
Wow, that is one disgusting miracle.

135
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:05,400
Start pushing. Here we go.

136
00:08:05,570 --> 00:08:07,400
Here come the shoulders.

137
00:08:14,030 --> 00:08:15,780
It's a boy.

138
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:19,300
- Is he okay? - He's just fine.

139
00:08:19,530 --> 00:08:21,070
You did it.

140
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:23,090
It's a baby.

141
00:08:23,090 --> 00:08:25,610
A beautiful little baby.

142
00:08:25,610 --> 00:08:28,910
And some other stuff I'm gonna pretend I don't see.

143
00:08:31,090 --> 00:08:34,220
- Would you like to cut the umbilical cord? - Okay.

144
00:08:38,010 --> 00:08:39,750
Well, that's spongy.

145
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:46,080
Hey, handsome.

146
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:48,940
I'll love you so much that

147
00:08:48,940 --> 00:08:51,990
no woman is ever gonna be good enough for you.

148
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:56,760
- We are so lucky. - I know.

149
00:08:58,310 --> 00:09:00,170
He has your eyes.

150
00:09:01,890 --> 00:09:03,590
I mean, I know that's not possible,

151
00:09:03,590 --> 00:09:05,620
but he does.

152
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:08,030
We'll just get him cleaned up a bit.

153
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:12,980
Oh, my God, he's beautiful.

154
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:15,140
Thank you so much.

155
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:17,680
I'm really happy for you guys.

156
00:09:17,710 --> 00:09:20,860
- How do you feel? - I'm tired.

157
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:22,960
You don't have that much time to relax.

158
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:25,300
The other one will be along in a minute.

159
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:34,160
I'm sorry, who should be along in a what, now?

160
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:38,540
The next baby should be along in a minute.

161
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:40,810
We only ordered one.

162
00:09:42,430 --> 00:09:45,610
- You know it's twins, right? - Oh, yeah.

163
00:09:45,610 --> 00:09:48,610
These are the faces of two people in the know.

164
00:09:54,710 --> 00:09:57,270
I can't believe you didn't know it's twins.

165
00:09:57,270 --> 00:09:58,580
This has never happened before.

166
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:02,170
Well, gosh. That makes me feel so special and good.

167
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:04,370
Wait. Did you know it was twins?

168
00:10:04,370 --> 00:10:07,340
It's here in the paperwork we got from the clinic in Ohio.

169
00:10:07,350 --> 00:10:10,460
- Did anybody tell you? - I don't think so.

170
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:13,490
They did mention two heartbeats,

171
00:10:13,490 --> 00:10:15,680
but l thought it was just mine and the baby's.

172
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:17,530
They said, "Both heartbeats are strong."

173
00:10:17,530 --> 00:10:20,380
And I thought, "Well, that's good, because I'm having a baby."

174
00:10:22,380 --> 00:10:23,700
This is unbelievable.

175
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:25,450
Twins actually run in my family.

176
00:10:25,450 --> 00:10:26,990
Interesting.

177
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,390
Can I see you for a second?

178
00:10:33,050 --> 00:10:34,130
What do we do?

179
00:10:34,130 --> 00:10:35,400
What do you mean, "What do we do?"

180
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,870
Twins!

181
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,990
Twins!

182
00:10:39,690 --> 00:10:41,800
Chandler, you're panicking.

183
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,780
Join me, won't you?

184
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:46,090
What do you say we keep one

185
00:10:46,090 --> 00:10:49,150
and then just have an option on the other one?

186
00:10:49,250 --> 00:10:51,860
- We can't split them up. - Why not?

187
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:54,330
We could give each of them half a medallion.

188
00:10:54,340 --> 00:10:57,400
And then years later, they'll find each other...

189
00:10:59,390 --> 00:11:01,420
...and be reunited.

190
00:11:01,510 --> 00:11:03,880
I mean, that's a great day for everybody.

191
00:11:04,630 --> 00:11:07,220
What if the person who adopts the other one is horrible?

192
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:08,650
What if they're not?

193
00:11:08,650 --> 00:11:10,410
What if it's adopted by a king?

194
00:11:10,410 --> 00:11:13,680
Yeah. Because I hear the king is looking to adopt.

195
00:11:14,170 --> 00:11:17,150
Monica, we are not ready to have two babies.

196
00:11:17,150 --> 00:11:19,080
That doesn't matter.

197
00:11:19,110 --> 00:11:21,000
We have waited so long for this.

198
00:11:21,010 --> 00:11:22,770
I don't care if it's two babies.

199
00:11:22,770 --> 00:11:24,300
I don't care if it's three babies.

200
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:28,550
I don't care if the entire cast of "Eight Is Enough" comes out of there.

201
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:30,980
We are taking them home

202
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:33,220
because they are our children.

203
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,870
Okay.

204
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,390
- Okay. - Okay!

205
00:11:38,390 --> 00:11:39,800
Okay.

206
00:11:40,870 --> 00:11:43,190
It looks like we're about ready over here.

207
00:11:43,190 --> 00:11:44,170
Come on, Erica.

208
00:11:44,170 --> 00:11:45,800
Start pushing again now.

209
00:11:47,260 --> 00:11:51,280
- Here she comes. - She? It's a girl?

210
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:52,620
Yeah.

211
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:56,820
Well, now we have one of each.

212
00:11:57,910 --> 00:11:59,620
And that's enough.

213
00:12:03,310 --> 00:12:07,090
And then she said it was the perfect way to say goodbye.

214
00:12:07,420 --> 00:12:10,450
Oh, my God. What did you say?

215
00:12:10,450 --> 00:12:12,540
Nothing. What do you say to that?

216
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:15,160
You've got to tell her how you feel.

217
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:18,030
- No way. - Well, you can't just give up.

218
00:12:18,030 --> 00:12:20,310
Is that what a dinosaur would do?

219
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:22,360
What?

220
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:25,100
Dude. I'm just trying to speak your language.

221
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:28,900
Ross, Rachel doesn't know that you even wanna get back together.

222
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:30,790
If she did, she might feel differently.

223
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:32,750
She might not even go.

224
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:35,660
- You really think so? - I'm telling you!

225
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:38,350
Oh, ok, this is the part of the musical

226
00:12:38,350 --> 00:12:41,060
where there'd be a good, convincing song.

227
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:48,450
Hi.

228
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:51,190
Can't a girl finish a song around here?

229
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:54,400
- Hey. - Hi. I dropped Emma off at my mom's.

230
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,510
- Okay. - You're not taking her tonight?

231
00:12:56,510 --> 00:13:01,270
No. We decided I'd set up, then my mom would bring Emma to Paris on Sunday.

232
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:03,260
Eight-hour flight with a one year old.

233
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:03,980
Good luck, Mom.

234
00:13:03,990 --> 00:13:04,770
You kidding?

235
00:13:04,770 --> 00:13:06,780
Eight hours with my mom talking about Atkins.

236
00:13:06,780 --> 00:13:08,410
Good luck, Emma.

237
00:13:10,810 --> 00:13:12,110
All right. You know what? You're right.

238
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:14,320
I should at least tell her how I feel.

239
00:13:15,210 --> 00:13:17,320
- Ross. Wait, wait. - What? What?

240
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:19,150
Could you get me a muffin?

241
00:13:22,810 --> 00:13:25,080
- Rachel? - Yeah?

242
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:27,710
I know you're leaving tonight,

243
00:13:27,710 --> 00:13:31,580
but I just have to tell you.

244
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:34,310
I love you.

245
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:40,140
Now, I don't know if that changes your plans at all.

246
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:44,740
But I thought you should know.

247
00:13:45,810 --> 00:13:47,490
Gunther.

248
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:51,620
I love you too.

249
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:54,480
Probably not in the same way.

250
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:56,210
But I do.

251
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:59,960
And when I'm in a cafe having coffee...

252
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:03,780
...or I see a man with hair brighter than the sun...

253
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:06,700
...I'll think of you.

254
00:14:13,550 --> 00:14:15,590
- Bye, you guys. - Bye.

255
00:14:18,910 --> 00:14:20,660
Oh, my God!

256
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:23,900
Unbelievable.

257
00:14:24,290 --> 00:14:25,170
Hey, you know what might help?

258
00:14:25,170 --> 00:14:27,610
I'm not getting you a muffin!

259
00:14:37,870 --> 00:14:39,310
Do you think they recognize each other

260
00:14:39,310 --> 00:14:40,780
from in there?

261
00:14:41,010 --> 00:14:44,330
Maybe. Unless they're like people who've lived in apartments...

262
00:14:44,330 --> 00:14:48,040
...next to each other for years, then one day they're pushed through a vagina...

263
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:49,680
...and they meet.

264
00:14:50,770 --> 00:14:53,420
We're going to take Erica to Recovery now.

265
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:55,880
There's something that we wanted to tell you.

266
00:14:56,980 --> 00:15:00,750
We decided to name the girl baby Erica.

267
00:15:02,070 --> 00:15:04,640
Oh, my God, that's just like my name!

268
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:08,880
Son of a gun, it is.

269
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,990
Anyway, I'm gonna go get some rest.

270
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:16,490
I'm really glad I picked you guys.

271
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:19,320
You're gonna make great parents.

272
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:21,220
Even Chandler.

273
00:15:24,190 --> 00:15:25,780
- Okay, well, bye. - Bye.

274
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:27,230
- We'll call you. - Okay.

275
00:15:27,230 --> 00:15:29,240
Have fun at church camp.

276
00:15:35,430 --> 00:15:38,520
- Look at these little bunnies. - I know.

277
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:41,400
You ready to trade?

278
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:43,610
- Okay. - Okay.

279
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:46,290
Okay. Let's see.

280
00:15:55,790 --> 00:15:58,190
- We could trade later. - Yeah, I'm good.

281
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:02,970
Hey, what are you working on?

282
00:16:02,970 --> 00:16:06,080
A "welcome home" sign for the baby.

283
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:09,460
How sweet! Oh, is that the baby?

284
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:11,990
No, I sat in the paint.

285
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:16,480
- Hey. - So did you talk to Rachel?

286
00:16:16,490 --> 00:16:19,590
- No. And I'm not going to. - What?

287
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:20,320
Why not?

288
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:22,160
She's just gonna shoot me down.

289
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,720
You guys saw what happened with Gunther.

290
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,040
That did not look like fun.

291
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:27,930
How can you compare yourself to Gunther?

292
00:16:27,930 --> 00:16:29,190
I mean, sure, he's sexy

293
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:31,340
in a more obvious way.

294
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:34,840
You have a relationship with her.

295
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:36,420
You slept together last night.

296
00:16:36,420 --> 00:16:38,580
Yeah, and she still wants to go.

297
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:40,960
It's pretty clear where she is.

298
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:43,100
I know what you mean. I mean, sometimes--

299
00:16:43,110 --> 00:16:45,480
- Joe. - Damn it!

300
00:16:46,250 --> 00:16:47,850
If I were gonna tell her,

301
00:16:47,850 --> 00:16:49,220
I don't have to do it now.

302
00:16:49,220 --> 00:16:51,780
Okay? I'll be seeing her again. We've got time.

303
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:54,480
No, you don't. She's going to Paris!

304
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:56,160
She is going to meet somebody.

305
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:58,980
Do you know how many hot guys there are in Paris?

306
00:16:58,980 --> 00:17:01,680
It's a city of Gunthers.

307
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:06,010
- Hey. - Hey.

308
00:17:06,010 --> 00:17:07,560
What do you have there?

309
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:08,860
Oh, I made a little something.

310
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:11,760
If I had more time to work on it, it'd be better, but....

311
00:17:13,910 --> 00:17:15,970
Oh, my God, you did that yourself?

312
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:17,720
Honey, that's gorgeous.

313
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:20,540
You know, the baby can't read, Mike.

314
00:17:22,350 --> 00:17:24,930
Hi. You guys. The car service just got here.

315
00:17:24,930 --> 00:17:26,650
I can't believe they're not home yet!

316
00:17:26,650 --> 00:17:28,220
I have to catch my stupid plane.

317
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:29,470
I want to see the baby.

318
00:17:29,470 --> 00:17:31,160
Monica just called from the cab.

319
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:32,620
She said they should be here any minute.

320
00:17:32,620 --> 00:17:35,260
Apparently, there's some big surprise.

321
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:37,140
Yeah, did she sound happy about it?

322
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:38,870
Because my friend Ethel's baby was born

323
00:17:38,870 --> 00:17:41,230
with a teeny-tiny beard.

324
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:48,890
- Welcome home. - Oh, my God.

325
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:53,750
- Oh, my gosh. - Hey.

326
00:17:53,750 --> 00:17:55,260
Hey.

327
00:17:58,250 --> 00:18:01,120
Hey, so, what is the big surprise?

328
00:18:05,190 --> 00:18:07,780
- Oh, my God! - How did this--?

329
00:18:07,780 --> 00:18:09,080
Okay, awkward question.

330
00:18:09,090 --> 00:18:11,720
The hospital knows you took two, right?

331
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:13,890
Yes. It's twins.

332
00:18:13,890 --> 00:18:15,320
Oh, my-- They are so cute.

333
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:17,990
Now, what kinds are they?

334
00:18:18,070 --> 00:18:21,060
This is a boy. And that's a girl.

335
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:22,860
Her name is Erica.

336
00:18:23,610 --> 00:18:26,140
Hey, that pregnant girl's name was Erica.

337
00:18:26,700 --> 00:18:30,590
Yeah. It's a shame you two didn't get to spend more time together.

338
00:18:31,810 --> 00:18:33,160
Yeah, and we named the boy Jack,

339
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:34,690
after Dad.

340
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:36,680
He's gonna be so happy.

341
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:38,740
Jack Bing. I love that.

342
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:41,130
It sounds like a '40s newspaper guy.

343
00:18:41,130 --> 00:18:42,780
You know, "Jack Bing, Morning Gazette.

344
00:18:42,780 --> 00:18:45,690
I'm gonna blow this story wide open."

345
00:18:49,910 --> 00:18:51,890
Oh, my gosh.

346
00:18:52,170 --> 00:18:54,010
So beautiful.

347
00:18:54,010 --> 00:18:55,510
I want one.

348
00:18:55,510 --> 00:18:57,740
Oh, yeah? Well, tell me which one.

349
00:18:57,740 --> 00:18:59,990
I'll try to slip it in my coat.

350
00:19:01,650 --> 00:19:02,830
Seriously.

351
00:19:02,830 --> 00:19:04,130
I mean, you want to make one of those?

352
00:19:04,130 --> 00:19:06,200
One? How about a whole bunch?

353
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:06,780
Really?

354
00:19:06,780 --> 00:19:08,890
Yeah. We can teach them to sing,

355
00:19:08,890 --> 00:19:11,590
and we could be like the von Trapp family.

356
00:19:12,090 --> 00:19:13,360
Only without the Nazis.

357
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:15,580
Although that sounds kind of dull.

358
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:18,290
I can't believe this.

359
00:19:18,290 --> 00:19:18,960
If I don't leave now,

360
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,560
I'm gonna miss my plane.

361
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:22,360
I'm so glad you got to see the babies.

362
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,230
Me too.

363
00:19:24,350 --> 00:19:26,490
I'm just sorry I'm not gonna be around

364
00:19:26,490 --> 00:19:29,420
to watch you two attempt to handle this.

365
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:34,720
All right. Oh, I can't say goodbye to you guys again.

366
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:37,470
- I love you all so much. - Love you.

367
00:19:37,470 --> 00:19:39,580
- We love you. - Call us when you get there.

368
00:19:39,580 --> 00:19:43,480
I will. Ross, come here.

369
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:48,040
I just want you to know...

370
00:19:49,570 --> 00:19:51,330
...last night...

371
00:19:53,050 --> 00:19:55,140
...I'll never forget it.

372
00:19:56,140 --> 00:19:57,740
Neither will l.

373
00:20:06,250 --> 00:20:08,400
All right. Now I really have to go.

374
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:11,580
Okay, au revoir.

375
00:20:13,140 --> 00:20:15,330
They're gonna really hate me over there.

376
00:20:17,990 --> 00:20:20,110
So you just let her go?

377
00:20:21,340 --> 00:20:22,730
Yeah.

378
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:26,810
- Hey, maybe that's for the best. - Yeah?

379
00:20:26,810 --> 00:20:30,150
Yeah. You know, you just-- Look, you gotta--

380
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:33,000
You gotta think about last night the way she does.

381
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,170
Okay? You know, maybe....

382
00:20:36,150 --> 00:20:39,870
Maybe sleeping together was the perfect way to say goodbye.

383
00:20:39,870 --> 00:20:42,110
Now she'll never know how he feels.

384
00:20:42,110 --> 00:20:43,840
Maybe that's okay, you know?

385
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:46,730
Maybe it is better this way.

386
00:20:46,730 --> 00:20:51,040
I mean, now.... Now you can move on.

387
00:20:51,230 --> 00:20:54,090
I mean, you've been trying to for so long.

388
00:20:54,090 --> 00:20:56,870
Maybe now that you're on different continents....

389
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:58,700
Right?

390
00:21:03,050 --> 00:21:05,090
Maybe now you can actually do it, you know.

391
00:21:05,090 --> 00:21:09,410
You can finally get over her.

392
00:21:13,830 --> 00:21:15,660
Yeah, that's true.

393
00:21:17,230 --> 00:21:18,670
Except....

394
00:21:20,950 --> 00:21:23,080
I don't want to get over her.

395
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:23,970
What?

396
00:21:23,970 --> 00:21:26,190
I don't. I want to be with her.

397
00:21:26,190 --> 00:21:26,900
Really?

398
00:21:26,900 --> 00:21:28,260
Yeah. I'm going to go after her.

399
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:29,970
Yeah, you are!

400
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:34,460
Wait! Wait! Get your coat! Get your coat!

401
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:36,440
- My coat. - This is so cool!

402
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:37,970
I have no idea what's going on,

403
00:21:37,970 --> 00:21:39,890
but I am excited!

404
00:21:39,890 --> 00:21:41,880
What do you think she's gonna say?

405
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:42,640
I don't know.

406
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:45,080
Even if she shoots me down,

407
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:47,230
at least I won't spend my life wondering...

408
00:21:47,230 --> 00:21:49,840
...what would have happened. Where is my coat?

409
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:51,880
You didn't bring one!

410
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,130
My cab's downstairs.

411
00:21:53,130 --> 00:21:54,400
I'll drive you to the airport.

412
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,950
- Wish me luck. - Hurry!

413
00:21:55,950 --> 00:21:57,270
Good luck!

414
00:22:08,390 --> 00:22:09,730
There's no seat belts!

415
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:11,580
That's okay. If we hit anything...

416
00:22:11,590 --> 00:22:12,880
...the engine will explode,

417
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:15,980
so it's better if you're thrown from the car.

418
00:22:16,980 --> 00:22:19,600
- All right, all right. Let's do this. - Okay!

419
00:22:21,470 --> 00:22:22,820
- Hey! - 80th and East End.

420
00:22:22,820 --> 00:22:24,220
No. I don't take passengers.

421
00:22:24,220 --> 00:22:26,390
The law makes you accept any fare.

422
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:28,710
You don't understand. This cab isn't real.

423
00:22:28,710 --> 00:22:30,760
What's your medallion number?

424
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:33,980
My medallion number is, get out of the cab!

425
00:22:33,990 --> 00:22:36,440
- What? - Get out of the cab!

426
00:22:42,860 --> 00:22:45,990
Oh, hey, can I give you guys my housewarming gift now?

427
00:22:45,990 --> 00:22:48,290
- Now, that you can do. - All right.

428
00:22:57,740 --> 00:23:01,590
Chick Jr.? Duck Jr.?

429
00:23:03,570 --> 00:23:06,010
Don't hide from Mama!

430
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:16,240
You can open your eyes now.

431
00:23:16,250 --> 00:23:18,510
- Are we off the bridge? - Yes!

432
00:23:18,510 --> 00:23:21,090
Is the old woman on the bicycle still alive?

433
00:23:21,090 --> 00:23:23,810
Yeah, she jumped right back up.

434
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:26,960
Oh, my God. Phoebe, slow down!

435
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:28,750
Do you want to get to Rachel in time?

436
00:23:28,750 --> 00:23:31,020
Yes, but I don't want to die in your cab.

437
00:23:31,020 --> 00:23:34,120
You should have thought of that before you got in!

438
00:23:35,410 --> 00:23:36,910
- Tollbooth. - What?

439
00:23:36,910 --> 00:23:38,710
Tollbooth!

440
00:23:39,460 --> 00:23:42,810
Four bucks. There are quarters in the glove compartment.

441
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:45,030
Hurry!

442
00:23:45,030 --> 00:23:46,520
Okay.

443
00:23:50,440 --> 00:23:52,730
Damn, that window's clean.

444
00:24:04,790 --> 00:24:07,190
We were wondering what was taking so long...

445
00:24:07,190 --> 00:24:10,420
...but now we understand. You were doing this.

446
00:24:12,990 --> 00:24:15,720
Okay. I wanted to surprise you, but....

447
00:24:16,140 --> 00:24:17,650
For your housewarming gift,

448
00:24:17,650 --> 00:24:20,540
I got you a baby chick and a baby duck.

449
00:24:21,030 --> 00:24:23,370
Really? You got us a chick and a duck?

450
00:24:23,380 --> 00:24:24,670
Oh, great.

451
00:24:24,670 --> 00:24:25,540
Just what you want for

452
00:24:25,540 --> 00:24:28,840
a new house with infants. Bird feces!

453
00:24:29,550 --> 00:24:30,910
But they must've jumped off the table.

454
00:24:30,910 --> 00:24:31,850
Now they're gone!

455
00:24:31,850 --> 00:24:33,080
Don't worry, we'll find them.

456
00:24:33,080 --> 00:24:35,470
Actually, I'm gonna go check on the twins.

457
00:24:36,180 --> 00:24:38,730
Oh, God! What did I just step on?

458
00:24:39,770 --> 00:24:42,080
It's okay. It's just an egg roll.

459
00:24:42,420 --> 00:24:44,510
You stepped on my egg roll?!

460
00:24:46,010 --> 00:24:46,650
I'm sorry.

461
00:24:46,650 --> 00:24:49,150
I didn't know to look for Chinese food on the floor.

462
00:24:49,150 --> 00:24:51,390
Just put it on a plate and leave.

463
00:24:55,350 --> 00:24:58,390
- Okay. Let's find these birds. - All right.

464
00:25:01,550 --> 00:25:04,190
Wait, wait. You hear that?

465
00:25:06,950 --> 00:25:09,020
They're in the table!

466
00:25:09,400 --> 00:25:11,510
Well, that can't be good.

467
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:13,880
- We gotta get them out of there! - How?

468
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:16,400
Maybe we can lure them out. You know any birdcalls?

469
00:25:16,400 --> 00:25:19,110
Oh, tons. I'm quite the woodsman.

470
00:25:20,450 --> 00:25:23,840
Well, maybe we can just tip the table a little.

471
00:25:23,840 --> 00:25:26,200
Joey, wait! The ball!

472
00:25:42,760 --> 00:25:44,330
So, what do we do?

473
00:25:44,330 --> 00:25:46,450
Maybe we can open this up somehow.

474
00:25:46,450 --> 00:25:47,800
Okay.

475
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:52,810
No. It's all glued together.

476
00:25:53,190 --> 00:25:56,260
Does that mean we have to bust it open?

477
00:25:56,260 --> 00:26:00,240
- I don't know. Maybe. - Oh, my God.

478
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:04,570
I know. It's-- It's the foosball table.

479
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:09,360
All right, you know what? We don't have a choice.

480
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:11,100
It's like I would have said in that sci-fi movie

481
00:26:11,100 --> 00:26:13,010
if I'd have gotten the part.

482
00:26:14,590 --> 00:26:17,760
Those are our men in there, and we have to get them out...

483
00:26:18,530 --> 00:26:22,030
...even if I have to sacrifice the most important thing in my life...

484
00:26:22,030 --> 00:26:23,890
...my time machine.

485
00:26:25,620 --> 00:26:28,600
- Did that movie ever get made? - It did not.

486
00:26:35,580 --> 00:26:36,760
Ross, where are you going?

487
00:26:36,760 --> 00:26:38,030
To talk to Rachel.

488
00:26:38,030 --> 00:26:40,990
Isn't that why we took a ride in the death cab?

489
00:26:41,210 --> 00:26:42,930
You're walking up to her at the gate?

490
00:26:42,930 --> 00:26:45,470
Have you never chased anyone through the airport before?

491
00:26:45,470 --> 00:26:48,400
Not since my cop show got canceled.

492
00:26:49,310 --> 00:26:51,560
You have to get a ticket to get past security.

493
00:26:51,560 --> 00:26:52,870
What? We're never gonna make it.

494
00:26:52,870 --> 00:26:56,170
Not with that attitude. Now, haul ass!

495
00:26:58,290 --> 00:27:00,080
Okay, if you could all walk slower,

496
00:27:00,080 --> 00:27:01,940
that'd be great.

497
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:12,750
- Madame, your passport, please. - Oh, my God.

498
00:27:12,750 --> 00:27:15,670
I was afraid I wouldn't remember my high school French.

499
00:27:15,670 --> 00:27:18,760
But I understood every word you just said.

500
00:27:19,230 --> 00:27:22,300
- Your boarding pass, please. - Oh, sure.

501
00:27:24,750 --> 00:27:28,660
Shoot, I had it. Oh, I can't believe this.

502
00:27:28,660 --> 00:27:29,820
Madame, if you don't have your--

503
00:27:29,820 --> 00:27:31,940
I have it, I have it!

504
00:27:33,970 --> 00:27:35,200
Okay, I can't find it,

505
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:39,080
but I remember that I was in seat 32C...

506
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:41,670
...because that's my bra size.

507
00:27:42,720 --> 00:27:44,020
Madame. You must have your boarding pass--

508
00:27:44,020 --> 00:27:45,250
Ok, fine. But you know what?

509
00:27:45,250 --> 00:27:48,900
If I was in 36D, we would not be having this problem.

510
00:27:55,790 --> 00:27:58,120
- Hi. I need a ticket. - Just one?

511
00:27:58,120 --> 00:27:59,270
I drive you here,

512
00:27:59,270 --> 00:28:01,340
and I don't get to see how it works out?

513
00:28:01,340 --> 00:28:03,890
Fine. Two tickets. I need two tickets.

514
00:28:03,890 --> 00:28:05,700
We're on our honeymoon.

515
00:28:07,350 --> 00:28:08,330
And the destination?

516
00:28:08,330 --> 00:28:10,890
I don't care. Whatever's the cheapest.

517
00:28:11,230 --> 00:28:13,360
I'm so lucky I married you.

518
00:28:15,500 --> 00:28:19,160
Oh, shoot. Damn it. Where is it?

519
00:28:19,860 --> 00:28:23,940
I found it. I found it. I told you I would find it.

520
00:28:23,940 --> 00:28:26,800
In your face. You're a different person.

521
00:28:27,910 --> 00:28:29,580
Sorry.

522
00:28:29,990 --> 00:28:33,410
Okay. Flight 421, Paris.

523
00:28:34,730 --> 00:28:36,030
I don't see it. Do you see it?

524
00:28:36,030 --> 00:28:37,230
No. Did we miss it?

525
00:28:37,240 --> 00:28:40,630
No, no, it's impossible. It doesn't leave for another 20 minutes.

526
00:28:40,750 --> 00:28:43,000
Maybe we have the flight number wrong.

527
00:28:43,600 --> 00:28:44,990
God.

528
00:28:47,730 --> 00:28:49,530
- Hello. - Hey, it's me. Here's Ross.

529
00:28:49,530 --> 00:28:50,840
What?

530
00:28:52,180 --> 00:28:53,410
Hey. Hey, listen--

531
00:28:53,410 --> 00:28:56,700
You wouldn't believe the cute noises the twins are making.

532
00:28:56,700 --> 00:28:57,550
Wait, listen.

533
00:28:57,550 --> 00:28:59,050
But Monica--

534
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:05,150
Monica...

535
00:29:05,810 --> 00:29:07,340
I'm sorry. They were doing it before.

536
00:29:07,340 --> 00:29:08,370
That's all right. Listen, listen.

537
00:29:08,380 --> 00:29:10,250
Oh, wait, wait. Here they go again.

538
00:29:11,370 --> 00:29:15,600
Monica...

539
00:29:15,600 --> 00:29:17,100
- <i>Monica? - Isn't that cute?

540
00:29:17,100 --> 00:29:19,540
That is precious! Listen....

541
00:29:20,540 --> 00:29:22,610
I need Rachel's flight information.

542
00:29:22,610 --> 00:29:24,220
<i>Oh, okay.

543
00:29:24,230 --> 00:29:27,820
All right, it's flight 421. Leaves at 8:40.

544
00:29:27,820 --> 00:29:29,910
Yes, that's what I had . It's not on the board.

545
00:29:29,920 --> 00:29:30,660
That's what it says here.

546
00:29:30,660 --> 00:29:34,190
Flight 421. Leaves at 8:40. Newark Airport.

547
00:29:34,190 --> 00:29:36,840
- What? - Newark Airport.

548
00:29:36,930 --> 00:29:38,730
Why? Where are you?

549
00:29:39,720 --> 00:29:41,320
JFK.

550
00:30:10,750 --> 00:30:12,010
Don't worry, you guys!

551
00:30:12,010 --> 00:30:14,210
We're gonna get you out of there!

552
00:30:15,350 --> 00:30:19,190
And we're also gonna buy you tiny bird hearing aids.

553
00:30:24,820 --> 00:30:27,760
Okay. Here goes.

554
00:30:32,780 --> 00:30:34,210
What's the matter?

555
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:38,500
I need to say goodbye to the table first.

556
00:30:40,150 --> 00:30:41,670
I understand.

557
00:30:42,930 --> 00:30:44,290
Okay.

558
00:30:47,870 --> 00:30:49,290
Table...

559
00:30:52,100 --> 00:30:56,470
...you have given us so many great times.

560
00:30:56,970 --> 00:31:03,240
And you guys, Jordan, Victor, Joel....

561
00:31:04,080 --> 00:31:06,720
All of you guys. What can I say?

562
00:31:07,590 --> 00:31:13,070
You guys make us look good.

563
00:31:16,430 --> 00:31:19,010
- You want to say anything? - I don't know.

564
00:31:20,870 --> 00:31:24,880
Except that, for one last time....

565
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:30,410
Good game...

566
00:31:32,570 --> 00:31:34,020
Good game.

567
00:31:37,660 --> 00:31:39,270
Okay. Here we go.

568
00:31:47,800 --> 00:31:49,440
I can't do it.

569
00:31:50,390 --> 00:31:52,340
Well, I can't do it either.

570
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:54,230
Hey. Did you find them?

571
00:31:54,230 --> 00:31:56,380
Yeah. They're stuck inside the table.

572
00:31:56,390 --> 00:31:59,200
And we have to bust it open, but neither of us can do it.

573
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:04,000
Oh, well, sure. It's got to be so hard.

574
00:32:04,660 --> 00:32:06,480
I'll do it. Give me.

575
00:32:11,830 --> 00:32:13,390
Phoebe!

576
00:32:13,680 --> 00:32:15,370
No, no, no!

577
00:32:17,030 --> 00:32:19,800
Wow, I've never gone this fast before.

578
00:32:20,070 --> 00:32:21,470
Phoebe, forget it, okay?

579
00:32:21,470 --> 00:32:23,500
Newark is, like, an hour away.

580
00:32:23,500 --> 00:32:25,240
There's no way we'll make it in time.

581
00:32:25,240 --> 00:32:27,200
She's got her cell. You could call her.

582
00:32:27,200 --> 00:32:29,170
I am not doing this over the phone.

583
00:32:29,170 --> 00:32:31,600
You don't have any other choice.

584
00:32:38,470 --> 00:32:40,600
- Hello? - Rachel. Oh, good.

585
00:32:40,600 --> 00:32:42,730
By the way, did you just get on the plane?

586
00:32:42,730 --> 00:32:44,950
- Yeah. - For what is worse, we would have caught her...

587
00:32:44,950 --> 00:32:46,860
...if we were at the right airport.

588
00:32:49,100 --> 00:32:53,550
- Rachel, hang on. - <i>No. No. No.

589
00:32:53,550 --> 00:32:55,730
Phoebe, is everything okay?

590
00:32:57,760 --> 00:33:02,400
Actually, no. No. You have to get off the plane.

591
00:33:02,410 --> 00:33:04,740
- What? Why? - I have this feeling that...

592
00:33:04,740 --> 00:33:06,090
...something's wrong with it.

593
00:33:06,090 --> 00:33:10,730
Something is wrong with the left phalange.

594
00:33:12,380 --> 00:33:15,480
Oh, honey, I'm sure there's nothing wrong with the plane.

595
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:16,530
Look, I have to go.

596
00:33:16,530 --> 00:33:20,440
I love you, and l will call you the minute I get to Paris.

597
00:33:23,440 --> 00:33:24,470
What was that?

598
00:33:24,470 --> 00:33:26,780
Oh, that was just my crazy friend.

599
00:33:26,780 --> 00:33:28,310
She told me to get off the plane

600
00:33:28,310 --> 00:33:30,400
because she had a "feeling" that there...

601
00:33:30,400 --> 00:33:33,900
...was something wrong with the left phalange.

602
00:33:34,830 --> 00:33:37,350
Okay. That doesn't sound good.

603
00:33:37,510 --> 00:33:38,500
Oh, I wouldn't worry about it.

604
00:33:38,500 --> 00:33:39,880
She comes up with this stuff,

605
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:41,330
and she's almost never right.

606
00:33:41,330 --> 00:33:43,300
But she is sometimes.

607
00:33:43,300 --> 00:33:44,660
Well....

608
00:33:46,520 --> 00:33:47,380
What are you doing?

609
00:33:47,380 --> 00:33:48,760
I can't take this plane now.

610
00:33:48,760 --> 00:33:50,510
Excuse me, sir. Where are you going?

611
00:33:50,510 --> 00:33:52,100
I have to get off this plane.

612
00:33:52,100 --> 00:33:54,510
Her friend has a feeling

613
00:33:54,510 --> 00:33:57,210
something's wrong with the left phalange.

614
00:34:00,980 --> 00:34:03,040
Could I get some peanuts?

615
00:34:03,980 --> 00:34:04,920
What's wrong with the plane?

616
00:34:04,920 --> 00:34:07,250
There's nothing wrong.

617
00:34:07,250 --> 00:34:08,360
The left phalange.

618
00:34:08,360 --> 00:34:10,180
There's no "phalange."

619
00:34:10,180 --> 00:34:13,480
Oh, my God. This plane doesn't even have a phalange.

620
00:34:14,380 --> 00:34:16,360
- I'm not flying on it. - Ma'am. Please sit down.

621
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:17,450
What's going on?

622
00:34:17,450 --> 00:34:20,790
We're getting off. There is no phalange!

623
00:34:24,940 --> 00:34:27,620
This is ridiculous. I--

624
00:34:29,630 --> 00:34:31,140
Yeah, okay.

625
00:34:40,050 --> 00:34:42,790
All right. My job here is done.

626
00:34:43,880 --> 00:34:46,580
That was impressive.

627
00:34:47,770 --> 00:34:50,320
Yeah. You didn't even use the tools for most of it.

628
00:34:51,460 --> 00:34:53,560
Yeah, they were just slowing me down.

629
00:34:53,780 --> 00:34:56,400
All right. I gotta get back to the babies.

630
00:34:56,400 --> 00:34:58,190
See you girls later.

631
00:35:02,120 --> 00:35:05,440
- Sorry about the table, man. - Yeah.

632
00:35:05,990 --> 00:35:07,600
You gonna buy a new one?

633
00:35:08,710 --> 00:35:11,400
Probably not. No.

634
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:12,820
I don't know how much I'm gonna want to play

635
00:35:12,820 --> 00:35:14,300
after you go.

636
00:35:17,760 --> 00:35:20,940
- At least we got these little guys out. - Yeah.

637
00:35:20,940 --> 00:35:23,600
We were worried about you.

638
00:35:28,130 --> 00:35:29,720
I guess I better get used to things

639
00:35:29,720 --> 00:35:31,950
crapping in my hand, huh?

640
00:35:41,180 --> 00:35:43,350
I'm gonna miss these little guys.

641
00:35:43,580 --> 00:35:45,770
It was nice having birds around again.

642
00:35:47,190 --> 00:35:48,690
Hey, you know what?

643
00:35:48,900 --> 00:35:51,080
Maybe we should keep them here with you.

644
00:35:51,410 --> 00:35:52,240
What?

645
00:35:52,240 --> 00:35:54,510
Yeah. We got a lot going on right now.

646
00:35:54,510 --> 00:35:57,190
And plus, here, they'd have their own room.

647
00:35:58,640 --> 00:36:00,640
I could get a goose!

648
00:36:02,520 --> 00:36:05,880
You know, I think you're set with the poultry.

649
00:36:08,590 --> 00:36:10,870
Thanks, man. You hear that, you guys?

650
00:36:10,870 --> 00:36:12,340
You're gonna get to stay here.

651
00:36:12,340 --> 00:36:15,000
And it's good...

652
00:36:15,070 --> 00:36:16,610
...you know, because....

653
00:36:18,090 --> 00:36:19,010
Because now you have a reason

654
00:36:19,010 --> 00:36:20,730
to come visit.

655
00:36:23,620 --> 00:36:26,430
I think there may be another reason.

656
00:36:34,670 --> 00:36:36,080
So....

657
00:36:38,290 --> 00:36:42,920
Awkward hug or lame cool-guy handshake?

658
00:36:44,670 --> 00:36:45,220
Yeah, well, you know,

659
00:36:45,220 --> 00:36:47,460
lame cool-guy handshake.

660
00:37:05,880 --> 00:37:08,520
Ma'am, I assure you, the plane is fine.

661
00:37:08,520 --> 00:37:10,890
And you fixed the phalange?

662
00:37:12,120 --> 00:37:14,370
Yes. The phalange's fixed.

663
00:37:14,370 --> 00:37:14,890
As a matter of fact,

664
00:37:14,890 --> 00:37:16,730
we've put a whole lot of extra phalanges onboard,

665
00:37:16,730 --> 00:37:18,260
just in case.

666
00:37:24,380 --> 00:37:25,560
- Where is she? - I don't see her.

667
00:37:25,560 --> 00:37:28,290
- Rachel! Rachel Green! - There she is!

668
00:37:28,290 --> 00:37:31,130
Rachel! Rachel!

669
00:37:31,850 --> 00:37:33,350
Whoa, do you have a boarding pass?

670
00:37:33,350 --> 00:37:34,910
No. I just have to talk to someone.

671
00:37:34,910 --> 00:37:37,130
I'm sorry. You need a boarding pass.

672
00:37:37,130 --> 00:37:41,450
- No, no. But you don't-- - Rachel!

673
00:37:43,910 --> 00:37:44,500
What? Oh, my God.

674
00:37:44,510 --> 00:37:46,760
What are you guys doing here?

675
00:37:47,050 --> 00:37:48,910
Okay. You're on.

676
00:37:48,910 --> 00:37:50,170
What? What, Ross?

677
00:37:50,180 --> 00:37:52,310
Okay, you're scaring me. What's going on?

678
00:37:52,710 --> 00:37:55,800
- Okay. Thing is.... - Yeah.

679
00:37:56,390 --> 00:37:58,760
- Don't go. - What?

680
00:37:58,760 --> 00:38:00,300
Please, please stay with me.

681
00:38:00,300 --> 00:38:04,010
I am so in love with you. Please don't go.

682
00:38:05,050 --> 00:38:07,110
- Oh, my God. - I know. I know.

683
00:38:07,110 --> 00:38:09,110
I shouldn't have waited till now to say it,

684
00:38:09,110 --> 00:38:12,160
but-- That was stupid, okay? I'm sorry.

685
00:38:12,160 --> 00:38:14,060
But I'm telling you now.

686
00:38:14,060 --> 00:38:15,590
I love you.

687
00:38:16,280 --> 00:38:18,520
Do not get on this plane.

688
00:38:19,030 --> 00:38:21,750
Miss, are you boarding the plane?

689
00:38:21,840 --> 00:38:23,240
Hey, hey.

690
00:38:24,020 --> 00:38:27,990
I know you love me. I know you do.

691
00:38:28,990 --> 00:38:30,740
- Miss. - I....

692
00:38:30,740 --> 00:38:33,560
l.... I have to get on the plane.

693
00:38:33,560 --> 00:38:35,160
- No, you don't. - Yes, I do.

694
00:38:35,160 --> 00:38:37,720
- No, you don't. I do. - They're waiting for me, Ross.

695
00:38:37,860 --> 00:38:38,840
I can't do this right now,

696
00:38:38,840 --> 00:38:41,570
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

697
00:38:41,570 --> 00:38:42,970
Rachel.

698
00:38:43,960 --> 00:38:45,610
I'm so sorry.

699
00:39:01,040 --> 00:39:02,590
I really thought she'd stay.

700
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:04,100
I know.

701
00:39:04,990 --> 00:39:06,440
I'm sorry.

702
00:39:20,110 --> 00:39:23,300
Well, that's it.

703
00:39:23,560 --> 00:39:25,270
Everything's packed.

704
00:39:28,950 --> 00:39:30,530
This is weird.

705
00:39:30,650 --> 00:39:31,480
I know.

706
00:39:31,480 --> 00:39:32,830
Yeah.

707
00:39:33,300 --> 00:39:36,200
Does this mean there's nothing to eat?

708
00:39:38,020 --> 00:39:40,590
I put three lasagnas in your freezer.

709
00:39:41,650 --> 00:39:43,230
I love you.

710
00:39:46,990 --> 00:39:47,850
Hey.

711
00:39:47,850 --> 00:39:49,620
Hey. Did you guys make it in time?

712
00:39:49,620 --> 00:39:50,330
Yeah, yeah.

713
00:39:50,330 --> 00:39:53,900
He talked to her, but she got on the plane anyway.

714
00:39:56,210 --> 00:39:57,760
Where's Ross?

715
00:39:57,760 --> 00:40:00,190
He went home. He didn't want to see anybody.

716
00:40:17,930 --> 00:40:21,450
<i>Ross. Hi, it's me.

717
00:40:22,050 --> 00:40:24,250
<i>I just got back on the plane,

718
00:40:24,250 --> 00:40:26,520
<i>and I just feel awful.

719
00:40:27,180 --> 00:40:29,110
<i>That is so not how I wanted

720
00:40:29,110 --> 00:40:31,170
<i>things to end with us.

721
00:40:32,570 --> 00:40:35,120
<i>It's just that I wasn't expecting

722
00:40:35,120 --> 00:40:35,820
<i>to see you.

723
00:40:35,830 --> 00:40:37,710
<i>And all of a sudden you're there

724
00:40:37,710 --> 00:40:40,150
<i>and saying these things.

725
00:40:40,770 --> 00:40:42,340
<i>Now I'm just sitting here

726
00:40:42,340 --> 00:40:43,960
<i>and thinking...

727
00:40:43,990 --> 00:40:45,770
<i>...of all the stuff I should have said

728
00:40:45,770 --> 00:40:47,450
<i>and I didn't.

729
00:40:47,970 --> 00:40:49,480
<i>I mean, I didn't even get to tell you

730
00:40:49,480 --> 00:40:51,430
<i>that I love you too.

731
00:40:52,640 --> 00:40:56,610
<i>Because of course I do. I love you.

732
00:40:57,950 --> 00:40:59,460
<i>I love you.

733
00:41:00,630 --> 00:41:02,160
<i>I love you.

734
00:41:03,060 --> 00:41:06,920
<i>What am I doing? I love you.

735
00:41:09,630 --> 00:41:11,250
<i>I've got to see you.

736
00:41:11,250 --> 00:41:12,690
<i>I've got to get off this plane.

737
00:41:12,690 --> 00:41:14,130
Oh, my God.

738
00:41:15,300 --> 00:41:16,570
<i>Okay, excuse me.

739
00:41:16,570 --> 00:41:17,840
<i>Miss, please sit down.

740
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:20,000
<i>No, I'm sorry. I'm really sorry,

741
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:21,190
<i>but I need to get off the plane.

742
00:41:21,190 --> 00:41:22,720
<i>I need to tell someone that I love them.

743
00:41:22,720 --> 00:41:24,420
<i>Miss, I can't let you off.

744
00:41:24,420 --> 00:41:26,490
Let her off the plane!

745
00:41:28,170 --> 00:41:30,110
<i>I am afraid you are gonna have to take a seat.

746
00:41:30,120 --> 00:41:32,470
<i>Oh, please, Miss. <i>You don't understand.

747
00:41:32,470 --> 00:41:34,580
Try to understand!

748
00:41:35,340 --> 00:41:37,250
<i>Come on, miss, isn't there any way

749
00:41:37,250 --> 00:41:39,470
<i>that you can just let me off the--<i>?

750
00:41:39,470 --> 00:41:41,150
No! No!

751
00:41:42,230 --> 00:41:44,410
Oh, my God. Did she get off the plane?

752
00:41:44,410 --> 00:41:46,350
Did she get off the plane?

753
00:41:48,240 --> 00:41:50,310
I got off the plane.

754
00:42:01,020 --> 00:42:02,800
You got off the plane.

755
00:42:15,180 --> 00:42:17,020
I do love you.

756
00:42:17,680 --> 00:42:18,510
I love you too,

757
00:42:18,510 --> 00:42:20,620
and I am never letting you go again.

758
00:42:20,620 --> 00:42:22,800
Okay. Because this is where I want to be.

759
00:42:22,800 --> 00:42:24,130
No more messing around.

760
00:42:24,130 --> 00:42:25,480
I don't want to mess this up again.

761
00:42:25,480 --> 00:42:28,720
Me neither. We're done being stupid.

762
00:42:28,730 --> 00:42:31,460
Okay. It's you and me, all right? This is it.

763
00:42:31,460 --> 00:42:34,680
This is it. Unless we're on a break.

764
00:42:44,820 --> 00:42:47,330
Don't make jokes now.

765
00:43:07,180 --> 00:43:08,240
Okay, please be careful with that.

766
00:43:08,240 --> 00:43:10,720
It was my grandmother's. Be careful.

767
00:43:10,720 --> 00:43:12,120
Thank you.

768
00:43:12,380 --> 00:43:13,580
If that falls off the truck,

769
00:43:13,580 --> 00:43:15,860
it wouldn't be the worst thing.

770
00:43:27,910 --> 00:43:29,420
I know.

771
00:43:29,590 --> 00:43:32,090
Seems smaller somehow.

772
00:43:33,910 --> 00:43:37,050
Has it always been purple?

773
00:43:39,950 --> 00:43:42,020
Look around, you guys.

774
00:43:42,070 --> 00:43:44,230
This was your first home.

775
00:43:45,320 --> 00:43:47,620
And it was a happy place,

776
00:43:47,790 --> 00:43:51,110
filled with love and laughter.

777
00:43:51,530 --> 00:43:52,500
But more important,

778
00:43:52,500 --> 00:43:55,930
because of rent control, it was a frigging steal.

779
00:44:00,170 --> 00:44:02,980
Hey, do you realize that, at one time or another,

780
00:44:02,980 --> 00:44:05,570
we all lived in this apartment?

781
00:44:05,800 --> 00:44:07,720
Oh, yeah. That's true.

782
00:44:07,720 --> 00:44:09,730
I haven't.

783
00:44:11,370 --> 00:44:13,190
What about that summer during college

784
00:44:13,190 --> 00:44:14,640
that you lived with Grandma...

785
00:44:14,640 --> 00:44:17,080
...and you tried to make it as a dancer?

786
00:44:22,190 --> 00:44:24,440
Do you realize we almost made it 10 years

787
00:44:24,440 --> 00:44:26,410
without that coming up?

788
00:44:30,110 --> 00:44:31,750
Oh, honey, I forgot.

789
00:44:31,750 --> 00:44:33,710
I promised Treeger that we'd leave our keys.

790
00:44:33,710 --> 00:44:35,230
Oh, okay.

791
00:45:10,020 --> 00:45:12,930
- So I guess this is it. - Yeah.

792
00:45:14,900 --> 00:45:16,350
I guess so.

793
00:45:18,440 --> 00:45:20,830
This is harder than I thought it would be.

794
00:45:21,040 --> 00:45:23,020
Oh, it's gonna be okay.

795
00:45:26,270 --> 00:45:27,640
Come on.

796
00:45:34,660 --> 00:45:36,540
Do you guys have to go to the new house now,

797
00:45:36,540 --> 00:45:38,780
or do you have some time?

798
00:45:42,050 --> 00:45:43,740
We got some time.

